ht be able  to  change to a different form so i think if  you're at the point of retirement it's a  extraordinarily sensible thing to do to  look at your house and think  could i live in a smaller house if i  released  a quarter of a million pounds of equity  out of this house which is bigger than i  need to live in  that's a quarter of a million i could do  a lot of sensible  retirement planning things within the  financial  arena but really i want to defer to  charlotte on that question if i may  of course charlotte yes i mean  one thing i should say is that we're not  able to offer financial advice uh  per se on this paddle either martin or  myself but  um you know the question i think is 58  and  and that's actually very young in the  context of  how long a retirement might last so one  of the things that is definitely worth  making sure of is to make sure that  those retirement assets the retirement  port is invested  um there has typically been this idea  that  as you uh grow older and as you approach  retirement you would want your pot to be  more in fixed income assets  i would think about it a little bit  differently first of all  just remember that just because you  retire  it doesn't mean that all of a sudden  there's only now another five years for  those assets to last they need to last  probably another  30 years in the context of the question  of this evening so  i would say they need to remain invested  in again diversified as we've talked  about before in order to avoid  um you know specific idiosyncratic risks  so to remain invested in a globally  diversified portfolio of  principally equity assets um  and expect that that will be the case  over a reasonably long period until  you know approaching much later on in  retirement  the other thing that that we do which i  i see happen a lot and i really like  actually is to think about  what you're wanting from your pension  pot so for example  for some people they may be looking to  draw relatively ear